{"causes":["Mao Zedong's consolidation of power and the development of his unique Marxist-Leninist ideology necessitated a simplified, accessible text for mass dissemination.","The escalating political tensions and ideological campaigns leading to the Cultural Revolution created an urgent demand for a unifying and authoritative political guide.","Lin Biao's strategic promotion of Mao Zedong Thought within the People's Liberation Army from the early 1960s laid the groundwork for the book's initial compilation and distribution."],"effects":["The Little Red Book became a central instrument in the creation and enforcement of Mao Zedong's cult of personality across China.","It provided the ideological justification and slogans for the Red Guards' actions during the Cultural Revolution, contributing to widespread social and political upheaval.","The book's global distribution amplified the influence of Maoist thought on revolutionary movements and radical left-wing politics worldwide during the Cold War."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"mao-zedong","sourceName":"Mao Zedong","verb":"CREATES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Mao Zedong's extensive body of speeches and writings served as the foundational source material for the Little Red Book."},{"sourceSlug":"lin-biao","sourceName":"Lin Biao","verb":"CANONIZES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Lin Biao spearheaded the compilation and mass promotion of the Little Red Book, particularly within the People's Liberation Army from 1964."},{"sourceSlug":"cultural-revolution","sourceName":"Cultural Revolution","verb":"CAUSES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"The political climate and ideological imperatives of the Cultural Revolution directly led to the book's mass production and mandatory study after 1966."},{"sourceSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","sourceName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"cultural-revolution","targetName":"Cultural Revolution","context":"The Little Red Book served as the primary ideological guide and source of slogans for the Red Guards and the broader populace during the Cultural Revolution (1966-1976)."},{"sourceSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","sourceName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","verb":"OCCURS_IN","targetSlug":"beijing-china","targetName":"Beijing, China","context":"The compilation, editing, and primary mass distribution of the Little Red Book were orchestrated from Beijing, the capital of the People's Republic of China."}],"places":[{"name":"Beijing, China","role":"Center of Publication"},{"name":"Nanjing, China","role":"Early Military Distribution"},{"name":"Tirana, Albania","role":"International Adoption"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","type":"Reference article","slug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q36393","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quotations_from_Chairman_Mao_Tse-tung"],"tags":["literary work","Historical & Literary Texts","cause-and-effect"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.","summary":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung (Chinese: 毛主席语录, Máo Zhǔxí Yǔlù, 'Quotations from Chairman Mao'), widely known as the Little Red Book (小红书), is a collection of brief quotations from speeches and writings of Mao Zedong (1893–1976), Chairman of the Communist Party of China, compiled and published by the People's Liberation Army under the direction of Lin Biao (Mao's Defence Minister) and first distributed within the military in 1964. A mass civilian edition was published in 1966 at the start of the Cultural Revolution, and the book subsequently became the most published book in the history of the world: an estimated 5–6.5 billion copies were printed during the Cultural Revolution (1966–1976), making it by some measures the second most printed book after the Bible.

The Little Red Book contains 427 quotations from Mao's writings and speeches, organised by subject in 33 chapters covering topics such as the Communist Party, classes in Chinese society, the mass line, war and peace, imperialism, criticism and self-criticism, party discipline, and the cultural revolution. The quotations range from strategic political analysis to aphoristic wisdom, and the book was designed for easy memorisation and recitation: its physical format — small red vinyl cover, pocket-sized, with bold headings and short quotations — facilitated its use as a handbook for political education and as a ritual object in Cultural Revolution practice.

During the Cultural Revolution, possession and constant reference to the Little Red Book was mandatory across China — reciting passages, 'studying' the book in group sessions, and waving it at political rallies were obligatory practices. The book's status as a quasi-sacred text of Communist China — used for collective oath-taking, displayed in homes and workplaces, and treated with near-religious reverence — made it one of the defining objects of 20th-century political culture and a paradigm case of the state-directed production of a political sacred text.","subjects":["Chinese Literature","Modern Era","Mao Zedong","Chinese Communism","Cultural Revolution","Political Text","20th Century","Chinese History"],"frameworks":["STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS","CAUSE_AND_EFFECT"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":8,"significanceNarrative":"The Little Red Book was instrumental in shaping the ideological landscape of China during the Cultural Revolution, mobilizing hundreds of millions and contributing to widespread social and political upheaval. Its global dissemination also significantly influenced revolutionary and counter-cultural movements worldwide.","significanceCategory":"continental"},"_editLog":[]}
